    "post_rendered": "Given two odd natural numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/8/8a8555382bcea5ac158f287985f83d3efff24df9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" > prove that for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/0/080cdf1a66b431a1c1e83b6f921e81bc2b4ec770.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ n\\in\\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" > there exists <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/2/6724f0ca7104f526205b2d9deb717704cb9fa846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ m\\in\\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" > such that either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/8/a08b92b738e2e605cd9aed79586f30237c77cb94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ a^mb^2-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"67\" height=\"15\" > or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/9/9492d8d6497ed9b781293c8af4e43709bebe27e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ b^ma^2-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"67\" height=\"15\" > is multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/6/0768d10b544c69387e17f0a9bec9ff68cc2afcc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ 2^n.$\"  width=\"21\" height=\"12\" >",
    "post_canonical": "Given two odd natural numbers $ a,b$ prove that for each $ n\\in\\mathbb{N}$ there exists $ m\\in\\mathbb{N}$ such that either $ a^mb^2-1$ or $ b^ma^2-1$ is multiple of $ 2^n.$",
