    "poster_id": 334559,
    "post_rendered": "Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/e/42ecbfb5e7dd547c1e0ca2eeb4669f2cc7f1ae4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" > be a family of subsets of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/9/7a973feadf2bddfb97ae636c3904ebebe689b7b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=\\{1,2,\\dots,100\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"148\" height=\"18\" > satisfying the following two conditions:<br>\n<br>\n1) Every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a313bf06349648df7be807bee95b651604ce7a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99$\"  width=\"17\" height=\"12\" > element subset of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\"  width=\"13\" height=\"13\" > is in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f92c87cbac40851328f044a4fe9def4719965e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{C}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"14\" height=\"13\" ><br>\n2) For any non empty subset <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/6/40632cfa9abed7fa1fca0e0bc551bf804e16bdae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C\\in\\mathcal{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" > there is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d61924c6d10dc6a6237d228017af751ef1bd98a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c\\in C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" > such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/f/dbf0d09e5484892caaa3dfad6bce315f504692b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C\\setminus\\{c\\}\\in \\mathcal{C}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" ><br>\n<br>\nWhat is the least possible value of <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/6/ae6f9dc0f89c03c8dffa60e795dc76b3c4040fb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\mathcal{C}|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" >?</span>",
    "post_canonical": "Let $\\mathcal{C}$ be a family of subsets of $A=\\{1,2,\\dots,100\\}$ satisfying the following two conditions:\n\n1) Every $99$ element subset of $A$ is in $\\mathcal{C}.$\n2) For any non empty subset $C\\in\\mathcal{C}$ there is $c\\in C$ such that $C\\setminus\\{c\\}\\in \\mathcal{C}.$\n\nWhat is the least possible value of $|\\mathcal{C}|$?",
